# The Go unit test of every row must catch a table that charges what it must not even when the gate cannot: the fault edits M1-15 (OUR capacity failure, settled as risky/plausible with a skip token: free)
# into a charge of m1_own in BOTH the embedded rules.psv and the fenced block of the spec, so check-charge-table stays green, and TestDecide_Rows/M1-15 must go red. The control is the real tree, whose
# tests must all pass. The leg needs Go only (the workflow sets it up); no database.
GATE=charge-rules
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=go test -run TestDecide ./internal/charge/ (one case per row of the table)
CMD=GOTOOLCHAIN=local go test -count=1 -v -run 'TestDecide' ./internal/charge/
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestDecide_Rows/M1-15
